  "worked_solution": "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{\u2015}{XY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(4-(-4))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{\u2015}{XY}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{10}{2}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
